## Problem statement

We have several different clusters, so we cannot just write one URL in mobile (or any client) app,
we have to have some way to point client app to what cluster it has to use.

We have two ways of setting up application: manual, with user-defined values for URLs and 
login/password, and automatic, with OTP code. As of now (January 2026) login via code is hard wired
to cluster where code is generated and there are no ways to determine where it was generated.

Our SIP realms are not bound to clusters. All realms we are using are in a format
<client_name>.pbx-cloud.velvetel.net , again with no distinction between clusters.
We don't have global DNS service to automatically bind realm domains to clusters.
Because of that, we are not connecting to SIP or backend with realm URLs, but instead we are
connecting with cluster URLs.

## Solution 1

Create some global service, kind of load balancer, that will point client app to required cluster.
This service will be integrated with DNS and OTP codes generation. This service will:
- answer to account creation attempts from all clusters: it will validate if this realm is available
- provide DNS records to our dns servers via zone transfer mechanism (AXFR)
- will generate OTP codes by request from some external clluster
- will answer to mobile application requests with OTP codes, providing all required info,
  including not only sip credentials, but also URLs for SIP, backend, etc...

### Pros:

- no need to update client applications when we create new cluster
- all DNS records bound to realms and pointing to real cluster, easy to use from all clients,
  be it hardware phone, mobile app or Creatio.

### Cons:

- longest to implement
- some initial efforts to make realms across clusters consistent
- Single point of failure

## Solution 2

Rework manual setup, make it with these fields:
- SIP realm (required)
- SIP username (required)
- SIP password (required)
- PROXY (optional)

```pseudocode
const server = proxy ? proxy : realm
const wss_url = 'wss://{server}:5065'
const backend_url = 'https://{server}'
```

Add prefix to code generation. Hardwire prefix values in both server configurations and mobile application,
e.g.:

'0' - staging   pbx-staging
'1' - prod US   api: portal-us.pbx-cloud.velvetel.net   sip: portal-us.pbx-cloud.velvetel.net
'2' - prod EU   api: portal-eu.pbx-cloud.velvetel.net   sip: portal-eu.pbx-cloud.velvetel.net
'3' - prod SEA  api: portal-sea.pbx-cloud.velvetel.net  sip: portal-sea.pbx-cloud.velvetel.net

In order to keep same level of security, mobile application should be updated, now we have 6-digits
codes, with prefix it will be 7 digits.

### Pros:

- easy to implement
- if setup correctly, nice and reliable

### Cons:

- need to reupload application to stores whenever cluster/prefixes configuration changes


